.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-engine-outdated 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-engine\-outdated \- Compare the config\*(Aqs release pin with the latest published release
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten engine outdated\fR [\fB\-\-notice\fR] [\fB\-\-record\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-releases\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-days\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare the config\*(Aqs release pin with the latest published release
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-notice\fR
Print one line naming `batten engine update` at most once a day, never in CI, and always exit 0
.TP
\fB\-\-record\fR \fI<record>\fR
Write the `engine\-fresh` line into this declared record family, judged by \-\-max\-releases and \-\-max\-days
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-releases\fR \fI<max_releases>\fR
With \-\-record: more releases behind than this is stale
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-days\fR \fI<max_days>\fR
With \-\-record: more days behind the first newer release than this is stale
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
